+++ b/openspec/changes/archive/2026-10-22-harden-patch-validation/design.md
@@ -0,0 +1,8 @@
+## Context
+
+`applyPatch` iterates with `forEach`, which skips holes, and reads members with plain property access.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- Iterate with an index loop so holes are visited and rejected by the existing "must be an object" check.
+- Read members through a helper returning `undefined` unless `Object.hasOwn`, matching the existing own-member check for `value`.
diff --git a/openspec/changes/archive/2026-10-22-harden-patch-validation/proposal.md b/openspec/changes/archive/2026-10-22-harden-patch-validation/proposal.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..1fd46a5de28359a201757527469b9811a75a34d5
--- /dev/null
+++ b/openspec/changes/archive/2026-10-22-harden-patch-validation/proposal.md
@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+## Why
+
+`applyPatch` accepts some patches RFC 6902 does not allow: a sparse patch array (holes) is accepted because holes are skipped, and operation members are read through the prototype chain rather than as members of the operation object.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Reject patch arrays with holes using a `JsonPatchError`.
+- Read `op`, `path`, `from` and `value` only as own members of the operation.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+- `json-patch`: stricter patch validation.
+
+## Impact
+
+`src/index.ts` (`applyPatch`) and `test/patch.test.ts`.
diff --git a/openspec/changes/archive/2026-10-22-harden-patch-validation/specs/json-patch/spec.md b/openspec/changes/archive/2026-10-22-harden-patch-validation/specs/json-patch/spec.md
