--- /dev/null
+++ b/openspec/changes/archive/2026-10-22-harden-patch-validation/specs/json-patch/spec.md
@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+## MODIFIED Requirements
+
+### Requirement: Validate the patch
+`applyPatch` SHALL throw a `JsonPatchError` when the patch is not an array, an operation is missing (a hole in the array) or is not an object, `op` is missing or not one of the six operations, `path` is missing or not a valid JSON Pointer string, `add`/`replace`/`test` lack a `value` member, or `move`/`copy` lack a valid `from` pointer. Only own members of an operation SHALL be considered; inherited properties are not members. Unknown extra members SHALL be ignored.
+
+#### Scenario: Invalid patches
+- **WHEN** the patch is `{}`, or contains `{"op":"bogus","path":""}`, `{"op":"add","path":"/a"}`, `{"op":"move","path":"/a"}` or `{"op":"add","path":"a","value":1}`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Sparse patch
+- **WHEN** the patch array has a hole, e.g. `[ , {"op":"add","path":"/b","value":1}]`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Inherited members
+- **WHEN** an operation gets `op` or `path` only from its prototype
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Null value is a value
+- **WHEN** an `add` has `"value": null`
+- **THEN** it is valid
